<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal inflation 0.0 pct mo/mo in Sept.</title>
<headline>Portugal inflation 0.0 pct mo/mo in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portuguese consumer prices rose 0.0 percent in September after 0.3 percent in August to give year-on-year inflation of 3.4 percent after 3.6 percent previously, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>Average annual inflation, the government's yardstick, was unchanged at 3.3 percent compared with the previous month.</p>
<p> PORTUGUESE INFLATION	  SEPT 96	AUG 96     SEPT 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI rise		  0.0	    0.3	  0.2</p>
<p> Yr-on-yr inflation		3.4	    3.6	  4.0</p>
<p> Average annual inflation	3.3	    3.3	  4.2</p>
<p> Index (base 100 1991)	 132.0	  132.0	127.6</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 3511-3538254  </p>
<p>The figures were in line with analysts' forecasts.</p>
</text>
